---
// One entry point for every hand-drawn mark. Two illustration languages
// coexist here. The original abstract line-doodle set (mark-*) keeps
// currentColor strokes plus two named fills (butter sun, lavender blob), so
// it is correct in any context by construction. The newer Xiaohei character
// set (every svc-* icon, plus xiaohei-*) is multi-tone: it still uses
// currentColor for ink outlines, but mixes in literal hex accents for
// colours that do not need to invert, the var(--color-surface) token for
// paper and highlight fills, three dedicated tokens (--color-xiaohei-navy,
// --color-xiaohei-code-navy, --color-xiaohei-sky) for accents that do,
// var(--color-accent) directly (svc-icon-* only, where the source colour is
// already the brand blue rather than a bespoke illustration tone), and
// (xiaohei-about-hero only) var(--color-ground) for cutout shapes (eyes,
// mouth, spout highlight) that show the page background through the
// mascot's solid silhouette rather than a paper/card surface. A third,
// small set (icon-*) covers bespoke small UI marks generated fresh for the
// Contact page's channel row (mail, GitHub, LinkedIn, map pin, radar)
// rather than extracted from a character scene; like the original mark-*
// set these are currentColor-only, with no per-theme colour variation,
// because they are plain iconography rather than character art.
//
// Astro's SVG components are static imports, so the whole set is named here
// rather than resolved from a path at runtime.
